IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P4-gate`

-- P4-art-29-30: Article 29 (Application of a conformity assessment body for notification) and Article 30 (Notification procedure).
-- Article 29(4) and Article 30(2) were replaced by the Omnibus (consolidated lines 553-555 and 561-562, marker `▼M1 REPLACED`):
-- each is encoded in both versions and dispatches on the version in force on the date asked. The second paragraph of Article 30(2)
-- (the Commission's power to amend Annex XIV by delegated act) is machinery and is inert (reason 2, NOTES.md).
-- Every function takes `the date asked` first and answers NOTHING before Chapter III Section 4 applies (2 August 2025).

§ `Articles 29 and 30: the parties and acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `Art 29 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 29 conformity assessment body`
    `Art 29 notified body`

DECLARE `Art 29 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 29(1) submit an application for notification to the notifying authority of the Member State in which the body is established`
    `Art 29(3) provide the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary`
    `Art 29(4) submit the single application for assessment to the notifying authority designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation`
    `Art 29(4) update the documentation whenever relevant changes occur`

DECLARE `Art 30 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 30 notifying authority`
    `Art 30 Commission`

DECLARE `Art 30 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 30(2) notify the Commission and the other Member States of each conformity assessment body`
    `Art 30(3) provide the Commission and the other Member States with documentary evidence`
    `Art 30(5) enter into consultations with the relevant Member States and the conformity assessment body`
    `Art 30(5) decide whether the authorisation is justified`
    `Art 30(5) address the decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant conformity assessment body`

§ `Article 29(1): where the application goes`

-- src:548 | 1. Conformity assessment bodies shall submit an application for notification to the notifying authority of the Member State in which they are established.
@ref Art 29(1) (src:548)
-- Gloss: a body that wants to be notified applies to the notifying authority of the Member State where it is established.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the conformity assessment body has submitted an application for notification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been submitted to the notifying authority of the Member State in which the body is established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 29(1) the conformity assessment body has submitted its application to the right notifying authority` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the conformity assessment body has submitted an application for notification`
        AND `the application has been submitted to the notifying authority of the Member State in which the body is established`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall submit an application for notification to the notifying authority of the Member State in which they are established" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:548 | 1. Conformity assessment bodies shall submit an application for notification to the notifying authority of the Member State in which they are established.
@ref Art 29(1) (src:548)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 29 party` `Art 29 act`
`Art 29(1) the duty of the conformity assessment body to submit an application for notification` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 29 conformity assessment body`
         MUST `Art 29(1) submit an application for notification to the notifying authority of the Member State in which the body is established`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 29(2): what accompanies the application`

-- src:549 | 2. The application for notification shall be accompanied by a description of the conformity assessment activities, the conformity assessment module or modules and the types of AI systems for which the conformity assessment body claims to be competent, as well as by an accreditation certificate, where one exists, issued by a national accreditation body attesting that the conformity assessment body fulfils the requirements laid down in Article 31.
@ref Art 29(2) first subparagraph (src:549)
-- Gloss: the application comes with a description of what the body does, the modules and the types of AI systems it says it is competent for, and with its accreditation certificate if it has one.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the application is accompanied by a description of the conformity assessment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by a description of the conformity assessment module or modules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by a description of the types of AI systems for which the body claims to be competent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an accreditation certificate issued by a national accreditation body attesting that the body fulfils the requirements laid down in Article 31 exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accreditation certificate accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 29(2) first subparagraph the application for notification is accompanied as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the application is accompanied by a description of the conformity assessment activities`
        AND `the application is accompanied by a description of the conformity assessment module or modules`
        AND `the application is accompanied by a description of the types of AI systems for which the body claims to be competent`
        AND (   (NOT `an accreditation certificate issued by a national accreditation body attesting that the body fulfils the requirements laid down in Article 31 exists`)
             OR `the accreditation certificate accompanies the application`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be accompanied by a description ... as well as by an accreditation certificate, where one exists" (a bare "shall" not done; the certificate limb falls away where none exists)

-- src:550 | Any valid document related to existing designations of the applicant notified body under any other Union harmonisation legislation shall be added.
@ref Art 29(2) second subparagraph (src:550)
-- Gloss: every valid document about the applicant's existing designations under other Union product legislation is added.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a valid document related to an existing designation of the applicant notified body under other Union harmonisation legislation exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every such valid document has been added to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 29(2) second subparagraph the valid documents on existing designations have been added` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `a valid document related to an existing designation of the applicant notified body under other Union harmonisation legislation exists`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any valid document related to existing designations ... shall be added": with no such document nothing is to be added (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `every such valid document has been added to the application`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be added" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 29(3): documentary evidence where there is no accreditation certificate`

-- src:551 | 3. Where the conformity assessment body concerned cannot provide an accreditation certificate, it shall provide the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary for the verification, recognition and regular monitoring of its compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 31.
@ref Art 29(3) (src:551)
-- Gloss: a body with no accreditation certificate must give the authority all the paperwork needed to check, recognise and keep monitoring its compliance with Article 31.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the conformity assessment body cannot provide an accreditation certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has provided the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary for the verification, recognition and regular monitoring of its compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 29(3) the conformity assessment body has provided the documentary evidence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the conformity assessment body cannot provide an accreditation certificate`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the conformity assessment body concerned cannot provide an accreditation certificate" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the body has provided the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary for the verification, recognition and regular monitoring of its compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 31`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall provide the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:551 | 3. Where the conformity assessment body concerned cannot provide an accreditation certificate, it shall provide the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary for the verification, recognition and regular monitoring of its compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 31.
@ref Art 29(3) (src:551)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 29 party` `Art 29 act`
`Art 29(3) the duty of the conformity assessment body to provide the documentary evidence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 29 conformity assessment body`
         MUST `Art 29(3) provide the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 29(4): existing designations; the single application; keeping the documentation up to date (replaced by the Omnibus)`

-- First subparagraph. The Omnibus changed "designated under" to "designated pursuant to" and "to support their designation procedure"
-- to "to support and expedite their designation procedure". The permission is the same on the facts the function takes (fork F-29-4).
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1075 | 4. For notified bodies which are designated under any other Union harmonisation legislation, all documents and certificates linked to those designations may be used to support their designation procedure under this Regulation, as appropriate. The notified body shall update the documentation referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article whenever relevant changes occur, in order to enable the authority responsible for notified bodies to monitor and verify continuous compliance with all the requirements laid down in Article 31.
-- VERSION as enacted
@ref Art 29(4) as enacted first sentence (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1075)
GIVEN `the notified body is designated under other Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents and certificates linked to those designations are used to support the designation procedure under this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
