         ELSE JUST `the notifying authority has provided the Commission and the other Member States with documentary evidence which attests to the competence of the body and to the arrangements in place to ensure that it will be monitored regularly and will continue to satisfy the requirements laid down in Article 31`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notifying authority shall provide the Commission and the other Member States with documentary evidence" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:564 | 3. The notification referred to in paragraph 2 of this Article shall include full details of the conformity assessment activities, the conformity assessment module or modules, the types of AI systems concerned, and the relevant attestation of competence. Where a notification is not based on an accreditation certificate as referred to in Article 29(2), the notifying authority shall provide the Commission and the other Member States with documentary evidence which attests to the competence of the conformity assessment body and to the arrangements in place to ensure that that body will be monitored regularly and will continue to satisfy the requirements laid down in Article 31.
@ref Art 30(3) (src:564)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 30 party` `Art 30 act`
`Art 30(3) the duty of the notifying authority to provide the documentary evidence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 30 notifying authority`
         MUST `Art 30(3) provide the Commission and the other Member States with documentary evidence`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 30(4): when the body may start to act as a notified body`

-- Two periods: two weeks where the notification includes an accreditation certificate, two months where it includes documentary evidence.
-- A notification that includes both, or neither, is not one the text gives a period for (NOTHING-kind, undefined term; fork F-30-4).
GIVEN `the notification includes an accreditation certificate referred to in Article 29(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification includes documentary evidence referred to in Article 29(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notification by the notifying authority` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 30(4) the last day on which an objection may be raised` MEANS
    IF `the notification includes an accreditation certificate referred to in Article 29(2)` AND (NOT `the notification includes documentary evidence referred to in Article 29(3)`)
    THEN JUST (`the date of the notification by the notifying authority` PLUS 14)  -- "within two weeks of a notification"
    ELSE IF `the notification includes documentary evidence referred to in Article 29(3)` AND (NOT `the notification includes an accreditation certificate referred to in Article 29(2)`)
         THEN JUST (`Art 28 to 39 the date the number of months after` `the date of the notification by the notifying authority` 2)  -- "within two months of a notification"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text gives a period for a notification that includes an accreditation certificate and a period for one that includes documentary evidence, and none for one that includes both or neither

-- src:565 | 4. The conformity assessment body concerned may perform the activities of a notified body only where no objections are raised by the Commission or the other Member States within two weeks of a notification by a notifying authority where it includes an accreditation certificate referred to in Article 29(2), or within two months of a notification by the notifying authority where it includes documentary evidence referred to in Article 29(3).
@ref Art 30(4) (src:565)
-- Gloss: the body may act as a notified body only if the Commission and the other Member States have raised no objection within two weeks (accreditation certificate) or two months (documentary evidence) of the notification. Read as: it may begin only once that period has run with no objection (fork F-30-4).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notification includes an accreditation certificate referred to in Article 29(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification includes documentary evidence referred to in Article 29(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notification by the notifying authority` IS A DATE
      `an objection was raised by the Commission or another Member State within that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 30(4) the conformity assessment body may perform the activities of a notified body` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE CONSIDER `Art 30(4) the last day on which an objection may be raised` `the notification includes an accreditation certificate referred to in Article 29(2)` `the notification includes documentary evidence referred to in Article 29(3)` `the date of the notification by the notifying authority`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): no period is given for this kind of notification
         WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN JUST (`the date asked` GREATER THAN `the last day` AND (NOT `an objection was raised by the Commission or another Member State within that period`))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may perform the activities of a notified body only where no objections are raised by the Commission or the other Member States within two weeks ... or within two months" (a list closed with "only")

§ `Article 30(5): consultation and the Commission's decision`

-- src:566 | 5. Where objections are raised, the Commission shall, without delay, enter into consultations with the relevant Member States and the conformity assessment body. In view thereof, the Commission shall decide whether the authorisation is justified. The Commission shall address its decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant conformity assessment body.
@ref Art 30(5) (src:566)
-- Gloss: if objections are raised the Commission consults the Member States concerned and the body at once, decides whether the authorisation is justified, and sends its decision to the Member State and the body.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `objections have been raised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has entered into consultations with the relevant Member States and the conformity assessment body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 30(5) first sentence the Commission has entered into consultations` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `objections have been raised`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where objections are raised" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the Commission has entered into consultations with the relevant Member States and the conformity assessment body`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall, without delay, enter into consultations" (a bare "shall" not done; "without delay" is an undefined term and gives no number of days)

